    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10442" root="خرق" body-key="x">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خَارِقٌ</span></b>  [act. part. n. of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خَرَقَ</span>]. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  [And hence,]
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَيْفٌ خَارِقٌ</span> <i>A sharp,</i> or <i>cutting, sword:</i> pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خُرُقٌ</span>.
(TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  [Hence also,] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَمْرٌ خَارِقٌ لِلْعَادَةِ</span> (assumed tropical:)  [<i>An
event breaking through,</i> or <i>infringing, the usual
course</i> of nature]. (KT, in a definition of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُعْجِزَةٌ</span>,
q. v.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  [In the present day, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خَارِقٌ</span> signifies also
(assumed tropical:)  <i>Profound,</i> or <i>penetrating,</i> in learning or science.]

